desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Dangerous Syscall"
	title_zh: "Dangerous Syscall"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-dangerous-syscall"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `dangerous-syscall` (ruby/lang/security/dangerous-syscall.yaml).
Original message: 'syscall' is essentially unsafe and unportable. The DL (https://apidock.com/ruby/Fiddle) library is preferred for safer and a bit more portable programming.
CWE: CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')
References:
- https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.rb": <<<POS
syscall
POS
	"safefile://pos.rb": <<<NEG
Fiddle::Function
NEG
)

${*.rb}.pattern_regex(/(?:syscall)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Dangerous Syscall",
	title_zh: "Dangerous Syscall",
	message: "Dangerous Syscall detected.",
}
